  "interiorEntryX": 10,
  "interiorEntryY": 13,
  "npcs": [
    {
      "id": "npc_sylvandar_thenna",
      "name": "Rootspeaker Thenna",
      "spriteName": "npcs/monk",
      "type": "QUESTGIVER",
      "defaultDialog": "The roots remember what the branches forget.",
      "questCompleteDialog": "",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "start",
        "nodes": {
          "start": {
            "id": "start",
            "text": "You feel it, don't you? The forest is... growing too fast. The bark reaches where it should not. I am Thenna, and I speak for the roots.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What's happening to the forest?",
                "nextNodeId": "explain"
              },
              {
                "label": "I'm looking for the Key of Roots.",
                "nextNodeId": "key_ask"
              },
              {
                "label": "Farewell.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "explain": {
            "id": "explain",
            "text": "Sylvandar experiments with a Shard of the old world. He tries to regrow what was lost. But growth without end is not life — it is suffocation. The vines strangle. The roots crush. People are... absorbed.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "How can I help?",
                "nextNodeId": "help"
              },
              {
                "label": "That sounds dangerous.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "help": {
            "id": "help",
            "text": "Investigate the spreading bark. The blight started near the Great Root and pushes outward. Find what feeds it. Then... you must choose whether to prune, or let it bloom.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'll investigate.",
                "nextNodeId": "accept"
              },
              {
                "label": "Not yet.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "accept": {
            "id": "accept",
            "text": "The roots will guide you. Listen to the forest, Unbound. Not everything that grows is good, and not everything that dies is lost.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I understand."
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_QUEST",
                "target": "the_spreading_bark",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "sylvandar_bark_quest",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "key_ask": {
            "id": "key_ask",
            "text": "The Key of Roots is not taken — it is grown. Only one who has proven their understanding of the cycle may claim it. Speak to the Amber Sage in Amber Grove. She holds the trial.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Where is Amber Grove?",
                "nextNodeId": "directions"
              },
              {
                "label": "Thank you.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "directions": {
            "id": "directions",
            "text": "North, through the petrified forest. Follow the amber glow. The Sage waits among the memories of the world before the Shattering.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'll find her."
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "farewell": {
            "id": "farewell",
            "text": "The roots are patient. They will be here when you return.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "x": 98,
      "y": 91
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_sylvandar_bloom",
      "name": "Bloom",
      "spriteName": "npcs/child",
      "type": "TOWNSFOLK",
      "defaultDialog": "...the bark is warm...",
      "questCompleteDialog": "",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "start",
        "nodes": {
          "start": {
            "id": "start",
            "text": "[A child stands before you, skin mottled with patches of living bark. Leaves sprout from her hair. She tilts her head.] ...you're not a tree yet.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What happened to you?",
                "nextNodeId": "what"
              },
              {
                "label": "Does it hurt?",
                "nextNodeId": "hurt"
              },
              {
                "label": "Goodbye, little one.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "what": {
            "id": "what",
            "text": "The forest wanted me. I was playing near the Great Root and... the roots held my feet. Now I'm partly a tree. [She flexes bark-covered fingers.] I can hear the sap singing.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Can you be cured?",
                "nextNodeId": "cure"
              },
              {
                "label": "I'm sorry.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "hurt": {
            "id": "hurt",
            "text": "No. It feels like... growing. Like spring inside my skin. Rootspeaker Thenna says I'm becoming something new. Not lost. Just... different.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "That's brave of you.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "cure": {
            "id": "cure",
            "text": "Thenna tried. Ashwalker Dren tried fire. Nothing works. Maybe I don't want it to. The trees are kind. They just don't understand boundaries.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Stay strong, Bloom.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "met_bloom",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "bye": {
            "id": "bye",
            "text": "[She waves with a hand that is half-fingers, half-twigs.] Bye! Watch where you step. The roots are curious about strangers.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "x": 105,
      "y": 95
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_sylvandar_dren",
      "name": "Ashwalker Dren",
      "spriteName": "npcs/ranger",
      "type": "QUESTGIVER",
      "defaultDialog": "Fire and forest... uneasy neighbors.",
      "questCompleteDialog": "",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "start",
        "nodes": {
          "start": {
            "id": "start",
            "text": "[A scarred man tends a small, careful fire in a clearing.] Another traveler. I'm Dren. I came from the Forged Isles seeking... penance.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Penance for what?",
                "nextNodeId": "penance"
              },
              {
                "label": "Can you help me with the overgrowth?",
                "nextNodeId": "overgrowth"
              },
              {
                "label": "Safe travels.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "penance": {
            "id": "penance",
            "text": "I was a forge-hand in the Crucible. We burned things that shouldn't have burned. I came here to plant fire-resistant trees — to prove that fire and growth can coexist. Pyralis and Sylvandar don't have to be enemies.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "That's noble. Need help?",
                "nextNodeId": "help_offer"
              },
              {
                "label": "Good luck.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "help_offer": {
            "id": "help_offer",
            "text": "If you're willing, I could use someone to clear the blight from my planting grounds. Kill the vine stranglers that choke the clearings, and I can plant my fire-oaks.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Consider it done.",
                "nextNodeId": "quest_accept"
              },
              {
                "label": "Maybe later.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "quest_accept": {
            "id": "quest_accept",
            "text": "You have my thanks, traveler. The vine stranglers lurk in the deep forest. Clear them out and this land may breathe again.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'll return when it's done."
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_QUEST",
                "target": "vine_strangler_bounty",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "overgrowth": {
            "id": "overgrowth",
            "text": "The overgrowth isn't natural. Sylvandar pours too much of himself into the land. He's trying to regrow the world — but a god's love is a heavy thing. It crushes what it embraces.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "How do we stop it?",
                "nextNodeId": "stop"
              },
              {
                "label": "I see.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "stop": {
            "id": "stop",
            "text": "Maybe you don't stop it. Maybe you teach it boundaries. Find Fungal Lord Mycos in the deep woods. He understands the necessary rot — that decay feeds new life. Sylvandar has forgotten that half of the cycle.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Where is Mycos?",
                "nextNodeId": "mycos_dir"
              },
              {
                "label": "I'll keep that in mind.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "mycos_dir": {
            "id": "mycos_dir",
            "text": "Follow the bioluminescent fungi southeast of here. Where the glow is brightest, you'll find his grove. Don't be alarmed by his appearance — he is more philosopher than monster.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Thanks, Dren."
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "bye": {
            "id": "bye",
            "text": "Watch the roots. They're always watching back.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "x": 85,
      "y": 130
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_sylvandar_mycos",
      "name": "Fungal Lord Mycos",
      "spriteName": "npcs/alchemist",
      "type": "QUESTGIVER",
      "defaultDialog": "All things rot. This is not tragedy — it is promise.",
      "questCompleteDialog": "",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "start",
        "nodes": {
          "start": {
            "id": "start",
            "text": "[A being of moss and mushroom regard you with ancient patience. Spores drift lazily from its cap.] Ah. A walker. Have you come to learn the necessary rot?",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "The necessary rot?",
                "nextNodeId": "philosophy"
              },
              {
                "label": "I need your help with the overgrowth.",
                "nextNodeId": "overgrowth"
              },
              {
                "label": "I should go.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "philosophy": {
            "id": "philosophy",
            "text": "Growth without decay is cancer. A forest that never sheds its leaves suffocates under its own weight. Sylvandar remembers only spring — he has forgotten autumn. The cycle requires both halves.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Can the cycle be restored?",
                "nextNodeId": "restore"
              },
              {
                "label": "Deep words.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "restore": {
            "id": "restore",
            "text": "Perhaps. My spores carry decomposition — the balance to Sylvandar's endless growth. Spread them at three blight-hearts in the forest, and the cycle may remember itself.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Give me the spores.",
                "nextNodeId": "spore_quest"
              },
              {
                "label": "I need to think about this.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "spore_quest": {
            "id": "spore_quest",
            "text": "Take these spore-pods. Plant them at the blight-hearts. But know this: decay is not gentle. Some of what Sylvandar has grown will die. That is the price of balance.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I accept the price."
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_QUEST",
                "target": "the_necessary_rot",
